-- The conventions (conventions.toml, the site's "מוסכמות" page) that are
-- arithmetic: one definition each, with the #ASSERTs that pin what it does.
-- A rule that applies one of them calls it from here (IMPORT conventions)
-- and never writes its own copy; tests/test_repo.py refuses a local
-- definition of any name this file defines. Changing a convention is a
-- change to its definition here, and every rule that calls it follows.
--
-- IMPORT reaches only the importing file's own directory, so each
-- collection directory holds a link to this file named conventions.l4, as
-- it does to the takanon's common.l4.
--
-- The conventions that are rules of reading (a qualifier's scope, which
-- provision prevails, …) stay prose: what they decide is which rule is
-- written, not a computation a rule could call.

IMPORT prelude

§ `מוסכמות הקידוד — הגדרה אחת לכל מוסכמה חישובית`

§§ `rounding.half`

-- Where the text says to round to the nearest agora or shekel, an exact
-- half goes up (0.5 → 1), not to the even neighbour. "Up" is toward the
-- larger number, so −0.5 goes to 0. L4's own ROUND takes a half to the even
-- neighbour (ROUND 2.5 is 2) and is not this convention.
GIVEN x IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `to the nearest whole` x IS
    FLOOR (x PLUS 0.5)

#ASSERT `to the nearest whole` 2.5 EQUALS 3
#ASSERT `to the nearest whole` 3.5 EQUALS 4
#ASSERT `to the nearest whole` 2.4999 EQUALS 2
#ASSERT `to the nearest whole` (0 MINUS 0.5) EQUALS 0
#ASSERT NOT (ROUND 2.5 EQUALS `to the nearest whole` 2.5)

-- The same, to the nearest multiple of a unit: 0.01 is the agora, 0.0001 a
-- hundredth of a percent written as a share.
GIVEN x IS A NUMBER, unit IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE x `to the nearest` unit IS
    `to the nearest whole` (x DIVIDED BY unit) TIMES unit

#ASSERT 0.12225 `to the nearest` 0.0001 EQUALS 0.1223
#ASSERT 2.5 `to the nearest` 1 EQUALS 3

GIVEN x IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `to the agora` x IS
    x `to the nearest` 0.01

#ASSERT `to the agora` 1.005 EQUALS 1.01
#ASSERT `to the agora` 1.0049 EQUALS 1
#ASSERT `to the agora` 167.7525 EQUALS 167.75
#ASSERT `to the agora` (832.62 TIMES 1.002) EQUALS 834.29

§§ `checks against a printed figure`

-- Not a convention: the arithmetic the checks use where the encoding sets a
-- computed amount beside one the text prints (rounding.printed-figure says
-- the printed one governs). An issuer's example that drops the third
-- decimal is reproduced by truncation; a comparison that forgives the
-- rounding of either side allows one agora.
GIVEN x IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `truncated to the agora` x IS
    TRUNC x 2

#ASSERT `truncated to the agora` 1.009 EQUALS 1
#ASSERT NOT (`truncated to the agora` 1.005 EQUALS `to the agora` 1.005)

GIVEN x IS A NUMBER, y IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE x `is within an agora of` y IF
    x MINUS y AT MOST 0.01 AND y MINUS x AT MOST 0.01

#ASSERT 9399.28 `is within an agora of` 9399.29
#ASSERT NOT 9399.28 `is within an agora of` 9399.30

§§ `dates.start`

-- A period that begins on a day ("מיום", "החל מ־") includes that day.
GIVEN d IS A DATE, e IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE d `is on or after` e IF
    DATE_SERIAL d AT LEAST DATE_SERIAL e

#ASSERT (DATE_FROM_DMY 1 9 2024) `is on or after` (DATE_FROM_DMY 1 9 2024)
#ASSERT NOT (DATE_FROM_DMY 31 8 2024) `is on or after` (DATE_FROM_DMY 1 9 2024)

§§ `dates.end`

-- A deadline, and the last day of a period ("עד יום"), are in it.
GIVEN d IS A DATE, e IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE d `is on or before` e IF
    DATE_SERIAL d AT MOST DATE_SERIAL e

#ASSERT (DATE_FROM_DMY 31 8 2029) `is on or before` (DATE_FROM_DMY 31 8 2029)
#ASSERT NOT (DATE_FROM_DMY 1 9 2029) `is on or before` (DATE_FROM_DMY 31 8 2029)

§§ `dates.school-year-share`

-- A share of a school year is measured over its twelve months, September
-- to August, unless the text sets another denominator.
`months in a school year` MEANS 12

GIVEN months IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `the share of a school year` months IS
    months DIVIDED BY `months in a school year`

#ASSERT `the share of a school year` 6 EQUALS 0.5
#ASSERT `the share of a school year` 10 EQUALS 10 DIVIDED BY 12

§§ `thresholds.above`

-- "מעל N", "יותר מ־N", "למעלה מ־N" do not include N itself. (Where the
-- text adds "לפחות" or "ומעלה", N is in, and the rule says AT LEAST.)
GIVEN x IS A NUMBER, n IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE x `is above` n IF
    x GREATER THAN n

#ASSERT NOT 50 `is above` 50
#ASSERT 50.5 `is above` 50

§§ `thresholds.until`

-- "עד N" of a quantity, a rate or an age ends at N and does not include it:
-- "עד 0.3" is below 0.3. ("ועד בכלל" or "כולל" include N, and the rule says
-- AT MOST; for a date, dates.end applies.)
GIVEN x IS A NUMBER, n IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE x `is until` n IF
    x LESS THAN n

#ASSERT 0.29 `is until` 0.3
#ASSERT NOT 0.3 `is until` 0.3

§§ `thresholds.shared-bound`

-- Where two rows of a table meet at one number, the number belongs to the
-- row that opens at it. A table read from the top row down asks whether a
-- value has reached a row's opening bound; a row read on its own is from
-- its opening bound up to, and not including, the next row's.
GIVEN x IS A NUMBER, bound IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE x `has reached the row from` bound IF
    x AT LEAST bound

GIVEN x IS A NUMBER, lower IS A NUMBER, upper IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE x `is in the row from` lower `to` upper IF
    x `has reached the row from` lower AND NOT x `has reached the row from` upper

#ASSERT 0.5 `has reached the row from` 0.5
#ASSERT 0.5 `is in the row from` 0.5 `to` 0.7
#ASSERT NOT 0.5 `is in the row from` 0.3 `to` 0.5
#ASSERT 0.49 `is in the row from` 0.3 `to` 0.5

§§ `thresholds.per-n`

-- A conversion "for every N" (pupils, hours, units) counts whole blocks of
-- N only: a remainder adds no block and is not counted in proportion.
GIVEN n IS A NUMBER, x IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `whole blocks of` n `in` x IS
    FLOOR (x DIVIDED BY n)

#ASSERT `whole blocks of` 25 `in` 60 EQUALS 2
#ASSERT `whole blocks of` 25 `in` 75 EQUALS 3
#ASSERT `whole blocks of` 8 `in` 7 EQUALS 0

§§ `position.above-full`

-- An amount "for a full position" is paid in proportion to the position,
-- above one position too, unless the text sets a ceiling.
GIVEN amount IS A NUMBER, position IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE amount `pro rata to a position of` position IS
    amount TIMES position

#ASSERT 1000 `pro rata to a position of` 1.2 EQUALS 1200
#ASSERT 1000 `pro rata to a position of` 0.5 EQUALS 500

§§ `amounts.increase`

-- "יגדל ב־X%" multiplies by (1 + X%), also where the quantity is itself a
-- percentage; it does not add X percentage points.
GIVEN x IS A NUMBER, rate IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE x `increased by` rate IS
    x TIMES (1 PLUS rate)

#ASSERT 1 `increased by` 12.5% EQUALS 1.125
#ASSERT 80% `increased by` 12.5% EQUALS 90%
#ASSERT NOT (80% `increased by` 12.5% EQUALS 80% PLUS 12.5%)

§§ `amounts.never-negative`

-- A payment of a difference is never negative and never becomes a debt of
-- the employee: below zero, it is zero.
GIVEN x IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `not below zero` x IS
    max 0 x

#ASSERT `not below zero` (100 MINUS 150) EQUALS 0
#ASSERT `not below zero` 50 EQUALS 50
